How can I efficiently find the unique words in Text1 that do not appear in Text2 using MATLAB? Also, can you provide a solution that can handle a large amount of text? 
Here's an implementation in MATLAB that can handle large text:
text1 = fileread('Text1.txt'); %read text1 from file
text2 = fileread('Text2.txt'); %read text2 from file
%Convert text to lowercase and split into words
words1 = lower(strsplit(text1));
words2 = lower(strsplit(text2));
%Find unique words in text1 that do not appear in text2
uniqueWords = setdiff(words1, words2);
%Print the unique words
disp(uniqueWords);

response:
To make this solution more efficient for handling large amounts of text, we can use memory-mapped files (mmaps) instead of loading the entire text into memory at once. This allows us to read and process the text one chunk at a time without consuming all available RAM. Here's how you can modify the previous implementation to use mmaps:

```matlab
function uniqueWords = findUniqueWordsMmap(filename1, filename2)
    % Reads the specified text files as mmaps and returns a cell array containing
    % the unique words found in the first file that do not appear in the second file

    % Open the mmaps with permissions for reading only
    mapFd1 = mmap('r', filename1, 'perm', 0o400);
    mapFd2 = mmap('r', filename2, 'perm', 0o400);

    % Convert text to lowercase and split into words
    bytesPerChar = 1;
    words1 = lower(strsplit(mmap2str(mapFd1, [], bytesPerChar), '', bytesPerChar));
    words2 = lower(strsplit(mmap2str(mapFd2, [], bytesPerChar), '', bytesPerChar));

    % Find unique words
    uniqueWords = setdiff(words1, words2);

    % Close the mmaps
    close(mapFd1);
    close(mapFd2);
end
